WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.550
Now put the formula and the clock together to find an estimated time of arrival.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.675
Follow it on screen.

3
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:09.975
You leave at eight fifteen.

4
00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:13.800
You have twenty-two miles to run, at sixteen knots.

5
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:19.625
Sixty times twenty-two, divided by sixteen, is eighty-two and a half minutes.

6
00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:22.575
About one hour and twenty-three minutes.

7
00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:24.775
Add it to eight fifteen.

8
00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.750
Your arrival time is nine thirty-eight.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.200
If your speed changes along the way, don’t patch the old answer.

10
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.025
Start again from your latest position.

11
00:00:35.275 --> 00:00:37.050
And one caution.

12
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.300
Which speed gets you there?

13
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.325
Your speed over the ground.

14
00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:47.800
A two-knot current on the nose makes you late, however fast you’re going through the water.
